# --- editor: .vscode is tracked ON PURPOSE ---
# The user-level global gitignore ignores .vscode; this re-include overrides it
# (a repo .gitignore takes precedence over core.excludesFile) so workspace
# settings stay versioned and new files under .vscode/ are not silently
# invisible to git status. Keep the contents limited to workflow settings
# (formatter policy, extension recommendations) -- no themes or fonts.
#
# There is NO workspace-level "machine-local" settings file: VS Code and
# Positron read .vscode/settings.json and nothing else. A
# .vscode/settings.local.json is silently ignored -- no error, no warning.
# Machine-specific values (R interpreter paths, fonts) belong in User settings.
!.vscode/

# --- Claude Code local state (.claude/settings.json is tracked) ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
CLAUDE.local.md

# --- delegation briefs for Codex: local process artifacts ---
prompts/*.md
!prompts/README.md

# --- R CMD check artifacts ---
/jmastats.Rcheck/
/jmastats_*.tar.gz
